# The Go image's build context, stated as an allowlist rather than as a list
# of things to leave out.
#
# A denylist has to anticipate everything that might ever sit beside the
# repository - an agent worktree, another project checked out alongside it, a
# cache directory the daemon is not even allowed to read - and it only has to
# miss one to ship a build that is slow, or surprising, or fails outright
# while transferring a directory nobody meant to send. The build needs five
# things; whatever else shares the disk is not the build's business.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!internal
!api
# Written by the release pipeline, and by a manual release, so the binary can
# report the tag it was built from. Absent in an ordinary build, where the
# Dockerfile falls back to "dev".
!VERSION

# Nothing under the allowlist may drag in a nested dependency tree, a git
# directory or a build artefact.
**/node_modules
**/.git
**/*.exe
